  "title": "Audit: auditable headline table (67 paper numbers copied from the final experiments and checked against their sources)",
  "assumptions": [
    "The plugin's metric-recompute check is only defined for an experiment's own primary metricKey; secondary numbers therefore need a separate audit record so the paper can quote them by ledger reference instead of by hand.",
    "Every copied value is compared against its source metrics.json inside the run; audit-mismatches must be 0 for the run to be meaningful.",
    "Q1/DATA-0002/TGT-0001 is the registration anchor only; the audit covers Q1, Q2 and Q3.",
    "No split is attached, so nothing here consumes SPLIT-0002 holdout exposure."
  ],
  "equations": [],
  "algorithm": "Audit/index only: reads the registered metrics.json of the eight final experiments as frozen dependencies, copies 67 headline/secondary numbers under stable audit keys, asserts every copy equals its source (fails on any mismatch), and re-derives six relations (Q1 baseline minus candidate, fusion minus graph OOF, Q3 projection cost, transfer Mahalanobis reduction, constraint-satisfaction gain, Q2 Jaccard gain). No model is fitted and no data is produced.",
